data: {"level":1,"reviewed":{"level":1,"label":"concept","text":"Applying `A` again and again tilts a vector toward the eigenvector whose eigenvalue has the largest\nmagnitude, because that component grows fastest. Normalise after every step so the numbers stay\nbounded. Once the direction has settled, the eigenvalue is the Rayleigh quotient `vᵀAv`, which is\nexact for an eigenvector."},"hints_note":null}

