data: {"level":3,"reviewed":{"level":3,"label":"code shape","text":"`v = rng.standard_normal(n)`, then `v = v / sqrt(v @ v)`. Set `eigenvalue = float(v @ (A @ v))`. Loop\nover `range(num_iters)`: compute the residual, break if it is small, then `w = A @ v`, break if\n`‖w‖ = 0`, and set `v = w / ‖w‖` and update `eigenvalue`. After the loop, find the first index whose\nmagnitude is within `1e-9` relative of the maximum, and negate `v` if that entry is negative."},"hints_note":null}

